{
  "contract": "estate-temporal-v2",
  "description": "Bi-temporal assertion-version vectors with closure records (VisionFlow ADR-2022 P1, contract v2). A version never carries an end. Valid time is the half-open interval starting at validFrom; recorded time is generatedAt. A closure record names a version and the clock or clocks it closes ('valid' = memory:ValidTime, 'recorded' = memory:RecordedTime, http://nova.dev/memory#, eljeffeg/memory-ontology, CC BY 4.0), carries validUntil iff it closes valid time, and takes effect from its recordedAt. Only v1 keeps the v1 form, an inline validTo, which is shorthand for a valid-time closure recorded at that version's generatedAt. replacedBy and reason are informative and do not affect state. A version is in state(t, recordedAsOf) iff generatedAt <= r AND validFrom <= t AND no closure of it that closes recorded time has recordedAt <= r AND no closure of it that closes valid time has recordedAt <= r and validUntil <= t, where r = recordedAsOf and an absent r means every closure applies. The first three versions and nine cases are those of estate-temporal-v1 and keep their answers. A case may carry expectValidTo, a map from version id to the reported end that the rule below defines (the earliest validUntil among the valid-time closures that apply at the cut, or null when there is none); only the ids listed are pinned.",
  "versions": [
    {"id": "v1", "subject": "urn:ngm:class:camera", "predicate": "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf", "object": "urn:ngm:class:device", "validFrom": "2026-03-01T09:00:00Z", "validTo": "2026-03-10T12:00:00Z", "generatedAt": "2026-03-01T09:00:00Z"},
